{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Problems and Solutions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "I Didn't Remember Having Met You Before"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe the reasons or results of events or actions in spoken or written texts, in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le12ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Perfect -ing Forms"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to talk about results and time, you can use a Perfect - ing form. You use this type of structure when you want to emphasize that one thing happens before another."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Having read your profile</span>, I think that we belong together."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In this case, the action that comes first is <span class=\"italic\">Having read your profile</span> . It is clear that the action <span class=\"italic\">I think that we belong together </span>comes last."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The form of the Perfect - ing is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Having + past participle"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at the examples from the text. Think about which event happened first."}, {"type": "example", "content": "After having received your business card, I went straight home and googled you!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've got to say, having read your profile, I really do think that the universe just wants us to be together. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, having cleared that up, let's talk about how we can arrange to bump into each other again, Boris. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reason Clauses: Because of, Due to, Owing to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " When you want to introduce a reason for a particular situation, you can use these prepositions at the beginning of the clause."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">because of </span>before a noun or a noun phrase."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">We won't be able to make it <span class=\"strong\">because of the weather."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Due to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">owing to </span>also mean <span class=\"italic\">because of</span>. They sound a little more formal, and are therefore more common in professional English rather than conversational."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She was unable to attend the meeting <span class=\"strong\">due to a previous engagement.</span><br>We have less money to spend <span class=\"strong\">owing to the budget cuts."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It's because of the name, really, that I knew we were destined to meet again."}, {"type": "example", "content": "He's a little bit discombobulated due to the long flight. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm befuddled because of a long one-hour flight."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I must have grabbed the wrong one, owing to all of the confusion in the reception area."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bump into "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to meet someone unexpectedly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Martina! I certainly didn't expect to bump into you here. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about a confusing situation."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flattering "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "making someone look or feel good"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She made a few flattering comments."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to mess around "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be silly; not serious"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Of course you're Adam. Stop messing around."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "discombobulated "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "confused and unable to think clearly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He's a little bit discombobulated due to the long flight. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to get something straight "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to understand something clearly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I just want to get it straight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "befuddled "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "confused"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm befuddled because of a long one-hour flight."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "flustered "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "upset and confused"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Wow, you really are flustered today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob06aud07"}